{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788596",
      "title": "Outputting List Content",
      "lectureOrder": 42,
      "videoOrder": 38,
      "sourceHash": "b18e2e2a0ddc9060756b5764be94b06aead95e28eac8f2f5b0f6ed33134cde19",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 1.92,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] Now I wanna come back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.92,
          "end": 4.68,
          "en": "to this list of users here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.68,
          "end": 6.15,
          "en": "We got a list of users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.15,
          "end": 6.99,
          "en": "That's nice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 6.99,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "but it's not really a dynamically rendered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 14.64,
          "en": "Instead, we're manually outputting for users here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.64,
          "end": 16.89,
          "en": "and we're manually controlling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.89,
          "end": 19.59,
          "en": "which user we're accessing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.59,
          "end": 22.86,
          "en": "And of course the problem with that is that in reality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "we have more than four users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 27.333,
          "en": "We have six in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.35,
          "end": 32.67,
          "en": "Now of course, we could simply add two more list items here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 35.58,
          "en": "but that would only help in this situation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.58,
          "end": 37.8,
          "en": "What if you're building an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.8,
          "end": 41.79,
          "en": "where you have a list of data that dynamically changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.79,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "where new items might be added or items might be removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 49.59,
          "en": "In that case, and also in a case like here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.59,
          "end": 52.17,
          "en": "where I don't wanna copy and paste",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.17,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "and set up all that code manually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 58.8,
          "en": "it would be nice to have some Angular feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.8,
          "end": 62.205,
          "en": "that allows us to dynamically render that list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.205,
          "end": 66.93,
          "en": "and that allows us to output as many list items as we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.93,
          "end": 69.51,
          "en": "for the data we have in a list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.51,
          "end": 72.36,
          "en": "And it turns out that such a feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.36,
          "end": 75.303,
          "en": "of course, exists in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 78.57,
          "en": "Here, in this unordered list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.57,
          "end": 81.69,
          "en": "instead of outputting all those list items like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.69,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "we can use a special Angular syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 87.12,
          "en": "to dynamically render that list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.12,
          "end": 89.825,
          "en": "And that syntax looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.825,
          "end": 94.825,
          "en": "@for, so almost like the for loop you know from JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.24000000000001,
          "end": 99.27000000000001,
          "en": "just with an extra @ in front of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.27000000000001,
          "end": 103.233,
          "en": "so that Angular can easily detect it in your templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "Then parentheses, and then user of users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 112.71000000000001,
          "en": "though this word here, user, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.71000000000001,
          "end": 114.63300000000001,
          "en": "You can use any name you want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.16,
          "end": 119.46000000000001,
          "en": "This word on the other hand, is not up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.46000000000001,
          "end": 124.46,
          "en": "This must refer to some property of your component class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.62,
          "end": 128.73,
          "en": "which holds the list data through which you wanna loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.73,
          "end": 131.31,
          "en": "So which holds an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.31,
          "end": 135.12,
          "en": "Then you add curly braces, opening and closing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.12,
          "end": 139.11,
          "en": "and then you put the code that should be repeated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.11,
          "end": 143.433,
          "en": "for every user, in this case between those curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.53,
          "end": 148.38,
          "en": "Now we can get rid of all these other list items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 148.38,
          "end": 151.29,
          "en": "because now they will be output dynamically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.29,
          "end": 154.56,
          "en": "at least soon because as you can see at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.56,
          "end": 156.75,
          "en": "we still got an error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.75,
          "end": 159.21,
          "en": "And the error I am getting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.21,
          "end": 163.683,
          "en": "is that such a for loop must have a track expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.36,
          "end": 167.656,
          "en": "This is solved by adding a semicolon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.656,
          "end": 172.656,
          "en": "after this first part of this for loop statement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 177.74,
          "en": "and by then adding the track keyword and then user.ID here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 179.07,
          "end": 181.14,
          "en": "And with that, the error goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.14,
          "end": 183.417,
          "en": "And I'll explain what this track thing does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.417,
          "end": 184.893,
          "en": "in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186,
          "end": 188.82,
          "en": "But with that, we're now replicating this list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 192.363,
          "en": "once per user in our user's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.77,
          "end": 195.78,
          "en": "And the individual user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.78,
          "end": 198.51,
          "en": "for which this item is being replicated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.51,
          "end": 202.14,
          "en": "is made available through that user variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.14,
          "end": 204.513,
          "en": "which is available inside of this for block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.44,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "And we can use this user variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 211.05,
          "en": "to then easily pass a specific user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.05,
          "end": 214.59,
          "en": "to every app user component instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.59,
          "end": 217.65,
          "en": "so that different instances of this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.65,
          "end": 219.603,
          "en": "receive different users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.37,
          "end": 223.77,
          "en": "With that, if we save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.77,
          "end": 227.88,
          "en": "you will see that we now have the full list of users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.88,
          "end": 232.88,
          "en": "and of course we got that result with way simpler code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 234.48,
          "end": 236.91,
          "en": "Now, what's the idea behind this track thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.91,
          "end": 238.5,
          "en": "which we had to add?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.5,
          "end": 239.67000000000002,
          "en": "Well, the thing is that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 242.88,
          "en": "of course we're dynamically outputting list data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.88,
          "end": 247.26,
          "en": "and Angular internally wants to keep track",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.26,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "of every item that is being rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 253.62,
          "en": "so that if the list input data would change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 253.62,
          "end": 256.41,
          "en": "if we would shuffle the list items around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 256.41,
          "end": 258.84,
          "en": "or remove some items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.84,
          "end": 263.84,
          "en": "Angular could easily reuse already rendered list items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 264.03,
          "end": 267.27,
          "en": "and doesn't have to recreate the entire list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.27,
          "end": 270.15,
          "en": "every time the list data changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.15,
          "end": 274.53,
          "en": "With this track expression here, we're telling Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 274.53,
          "end": 278.58,
          "en": "which unique identification criteria",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 278.58,
          "end": 283.58,
          "en": "can be assigned by Angular automatically behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.8,
          "end": 286.68,
          "en": "to every list item, in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 286.68,
          "end": 290.22,
          "en": "to every element it's rendering per user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.22,
          "end": 294.27,
          "en": "And here it's that user ID, which will be unique per user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.27,
          "end": 297.06,
          "en": "And Angular will basically connect that ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 297.06,
          "end": 299.1,
          "en": "to every list item it outputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 299.1,
          "end": 301.8,
          "en": "so that every list item has a different ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 301.8,
          "end": 305.61,
          "en": "and that then helps Angular update the list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 305.61,
          "end": 308.07,
          "en": "if the list data would change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 308.07,
          "end": 312.123,
          "en": "Ut helps Angular update that list in a highly efficient way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.05,
          "end": 314.52,
          "en": "Here it doesn't really matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 314.52,
          "end": 316.83,
          "en": "because users will never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.83,
          "end": 321.54,
          "en": "Nonetheless, you always must add such a track expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 321.54,
          "end": 325.05,
          "en": "But with that, we can now output list content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.05,
          "end": 327.24,
          "en": "And as you will see throughout the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 327.24,
          "end": 331.623,
          "en": "this is a crucial feature which you will be using a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
